.TH SNARKYCTL 1 "October 2026" "SnarkyCtl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snarkyctl \- administer the Snarkypuss private VPN gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snarkyctl
.RI [ --version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snarkyctl
provides local administration, configuration validation, preflight checks,
and status queries for the Snarkypuss VPN gateway.
Some operations communicate with the privileged SnarkyCtl control daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show current gateway and upstream VPN status.
.TP
.B preflight
Perform read-only deployment safety checks.
.TP
.B validate-config
Validate the main configuration.
.TP
.B connect
Connect to a configured provider target alias.
.TP
.B disconnect
Disconnect the upstream VPN through SnarkyCtl's control plane.
.TP
.B targets-db
Administer the provider target catalogue database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed SnarkyCtl version.
.TP
.B --help
Show supported commands and options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/snarkyctl/snarkyctl.yaml
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/snarkyctl/targets.db
Provider target catalogue database.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Snarkypuss administration and deployment documentation at
.UR https://github.com/topquark22/Snarkypuss
.UE
